Centering a `div` in CSS can be done in several ways, depending on your specific needs and the layout of your webpage. Here are some common methods:

### 1. Using Flexbox
Flexbox is one of the most modern and flexible ways to center elements.

```css
.container {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center; /* Centers horizontally */
    align-items: center;     /* Centers vertically (if needed) */
    height: 100vh;           /* Optional: sets the container height to full viewport height */
}
```

### 2. Using Grid Layout
CSS Grid is another powerful layout method that can be used for centering.

```css
.container {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;      /* Centers both horizontally and vertically */
    height: 100vh;            /* Optional: sets the container height to full viewport height */
}
```

### 3. Using Margin Auto
This method works well for block-level elements.

```css
.centered-div {
    margin: auto;
    width: 50%;              /* Set a fixed width or use a percentage */
    text-align: center;      /* Optional: centers text inside the div if needed */
}
```

